d3c9ea0b-e96c-451c-b8b6-fb789cb0245d	WILLIAM ODONNELL | REALTOR	uncontacted	\N	\N	\N	cb292d78-a16c-42f6-b3d7-6c93c3b9e49d	0f12cb2a-2ce3-4916-b175-0d5dcd529d15	2025-11-19 14:35:06.84104+00	2025-11-19 14:35:06.84104+00	985f8cd2-b1c9-4a06-a9ac-63f80d854f38	medium	open	\N	\N	USD	EST	\N	\N	\N	\N	0	\N	JL	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Rate Agreed Peviously: 15 | Hours: 20 | Notes: Here's the updated task list with a focus on transaction coordination, communication with agents, and the importance of being bilingual:\n\n### Task List for Transaction Coordinator\n\n#### 1. Transaction Coordination (Priority)\n- **Initial Transaction Setup**\n- Input transaction details into Command CRM as soon as a new deal is initiated.\n- Confirm all necessary documentation is received from clients and agents.\n\n- **Ongoing Transaction Management**\n- Monitor transaction timelines and ensure all milestones are met.\n- Follow up with all parties (clients, agents, and service providers) to ensure smooth progression of transactions.\n\n- **Closing Coordination**\n- Prepare and distribute closing documents.\n- Confirm closing details with all parties involved, ensuring clarity and understanding.\n\n#### 2. Communication with Agents\n- **Agent Liaison**\n- Maintain regular communication with agents involved in transactions to coordinate schedules and updates.\n- Provide agents with necessary documentation and updates regarding transaction status.\n\n- **Conflict Resolution**\n- Address any issues or questions raised by agents promptly and effectively.\n- Facilitate discussions between clients and agents as needed to ensure smooth communication.\n\n#### 3. Calendar Management\n- **Scheduling Appointments**\n- Organize and manage William’s calendar, including meetings with agents and clients.\n- Ensure no scheduling conflicts occur, especially during critical transaction periods.\n\n- **Reminder System**\n- Set reminders for key transaction deadlines and meetings.\n\n#### 4. Email Management\n- **Email Organization**\n- Monitor and categorize emails related to transactions, clients, and agents.\n- Draft timely responses to emails, particularly regarding transaction inquiries.\n\n- **Communication Follow-up**\n- Ensure follow-ups on important emails are done within 48 hours to maintain clear communication.\n\n#### 5. Command CRM Management\n- **Data Entry and Updates**\n- Regularly update transaction details and client information in Command CRM.\n- Ensure all data is accurate and accessible for reference.\n\n#### 6. Graphic Design and Video Editing\n- **Marketing Material Creation**\n- Design and produce marketing materials for listings, ensuring alignment with William's branding.\n- Edit promotional videos as needed for client engagement.\n\n#### 7. Bilingual Communication\n- **Client Interaction**\n- Conduct all client communications in both English and Spanish, ensuring clarity and professionalism.\n- Provide bilingual support in meetings and communications with agents, facilitating seamless interactions.\n\n- **Documentation Translation**\n- Translate documents as necessary to ensure clients and agents fully understand all materials.\n\n#### 8. Reporting\n- **Transaction Updates**\n- Prepare weekly reports summarizing the status of all transactions, client interactions, and agent communications for William.\n\n### Additional Considerations\n- **Emphasis on Bilingual Skills**\n- Leverage fluency in Spanish and English to enhance communication and relationships with diverse clients and agents.\n- Recognize the critical role of bilingualism in ensuring client satisfaction and smooth transactions.\n\nThis revised task list highlights the importance of transaction coordination, effective communication with agents, and the critical role of being bilingual in this position. \n1. **Transaction Coordination Skills**\n- Strong understanding of real estate transaction processes.\n- Ability to manage timelines and deadlines effectively.\n\n2. **CRM Proficiency**\n- Proficie